# First-time maintenance cutscene.
# Format: see data/dialogue/school.dlg. One line = one page (click to advance).
#
# Plays once, the first time the player picks Maintenance, before the
# maintenance scene itself loads (MaintenanceIntro.gd). Backgrounds:
# factory_outside on the first page, maintenance_stairs from the second page
# (MaintenanceIntro.STAIRS_PAGE_INDEX, whatever it says), then maintenance_hallway
# from the page containing "peer around the corner" (HALLWAY_CUE) to the end.
# The player sneaks into his uncle's factory without clocking in, so the
# cleaning robots won't recognise him as authorised personnel. One is cleaning
# right outside the PERSONNEL ONLY door he needs, until the head in his bag
# hacks it and sends it away.
#
# The cleaning robot is drawn over the hallway. The page containing "stops
# mid-scrub" (MaintenanceIntro.ROBOT_HACKED_CUE) turns its head, and the page
# containing "down the hall" (MaintenanceIntro.ROBOT_LEAVES_CUE) hides it. Keep
# those phrases in the lines if you reword them.

[intro]
[i]You arrive at your Uncle's factory.[/i]
Thoughts: There's a old room no one ever goes in where I can work on the bot.
Thoughts: I'll have go in from around back. But if I'm not clocked in, the cleaning bots will see me as an intruder.
Thoughts: If one of them spots me, it'll flag me as unauthorized personnel. Then I'll have some serious explaining to do to my Uncle.
No one seems to be in this part of the factory.
It's a repurposed building. Some parts of it weren't made for manufacturing purposes...
[i]You peer around the corner.[/i]
[i]There's a cleaning robot is scrubbing the floor outside a door.[/i]
Thought: Damn it. Of course it's cleaning right there...
Thoughts: That's literally the room I need to get into.
Thoughts: I'll just wait it out.
[i]You wait.[/i]
[i]And wait...[/i]
[i]And wait.....[/i]
........
[i]The cleaning robot loops back to scrubbing the same few tiles for the sixth time.[/i]
Thoughts: How long does it take to clean one spot of floor??
Thoughts: It's been ten minutes. That floor is clean. That floor has never been cleaner.
A voice comes from inside your bag.
Her: You know I can just move it.
[i]You nearly jump out of your skin.[/i]
You: Keep your voice down!
Her: It can't hear me. Its microphones are broken.
You: You sure it's just the microphones? Look at it. Something's wrong with its brain.
Her: It's as if it's made almost entirely out of spare parts.
You: Maybe I can take it down?
Her: "Take it down?" Are you serious?
Have you ever even been in a fight?
You: No, but I bet I could win if it came to it.
Her: Sure... But save your breath, I'll move it myself.
You: How? Youre just a head...
Her: I can hack it. Give it somewhere else to be.
You: From inside my bag?
Her: Watch.
[i]The cleaning robot stops mid-scrub. Its eye-lights flickers blue.[/i]
[i]Then it turns and quickly strides down the hall, and disappears around the far corner.[/i]
Thoughts: …Creepy.
Thoughts: If one head in a backpack can do that… I'm starting to get why these things were such a problem for us during the war.
You: Wait. How did you even reach it? Are you connected to the factory's wifi?
Her: …I am.
Her: That's odd. I don't remember connecting to it.
Thoughts: That's not reassuring.
You: We'll worry about that later.
[i]You head for the maintenance room.[/i]
